  "rationale": "Monk's second Columbia album captures his working quartet at peak cohesion after four years together. Revisiting classic compositions (Criss-Cross, Rhythm-a-Ning, Hackensack) the quartet had thoroughly absorbed, the album documents the band that supported Monk's Time cover-story profile in 1964. Penguin Guide, DownBeat, and Rolling Stone all rate it highly; AllMusic calls it 'some of the finest work that Monk ever did in the studio.' A defining statement of Monk's mid-1960s quartet sound and a consensus core collection entry.",
